00:33:15.610 --> 00:33:17.440
involved in creativity.

00:33:17.440 --> 00:33:19.690
But I want to be very
clear that any time we

00:33:19.690 --> 00:33:21.880
talk about mechanisms
and brain areas, what's

00:33:21.880 --> 00:33:24.430
far more important than the
names of those brain areas

00:33:24.430 --> 00:33:25.947
is an understanding
of what they do.

00:33:25.947 --> 00:33:28.030
So if you couldn't remember
the anterior cingulate

00:33:28.030 --> 00:33:30.160
cortex or the fact that
the prefrontal cortex is

00:33:30.160 --> 00:33:33.580
involved in executive function,
et cetera, that's fine.

00:33:33.580 --> 00:33:35.800
It's less important that
you know the names of things

00:33:35.800 --> 00:33:38.860
than you understand the action
steps that those things take.

00:33:38.860 --> 00:33:41.770
That is the verb actions
that those particular brain

00:33:41.770 --> 00:33:44.410
areas engage in order to arrive
at a particular endpoint.

00:33:44.410 --> 00:33:48.470
And the endpoint we're talking
about today is creativity.

00:33:48.470 --> 00:33:51.670
I want to discuss creativity
in terms of what actually

00:33:51.670 --> 00:33:53.110
goes into being creative.

00:33:53.110 --> 00:33:55.012
And it turns out there
are just two elements.

00:33:55.012 --> 00:33:56.470
And those two
elements are now well

00:33:56.470 --> 00:33:58.540
understood from the
perspective of psychology

00:33:58.540 --> 00:34:01.390
and fortunately, the
neuroscience well

00:34:01.390 --> 00:34:04.510
supports what the psychology
says and vise versa.

00:34:04.510 --> 00:34:07.480
And those two elements
that go into coming up

00:34:07.480 --> 00:34:10.929
with a creative idea and then
implementing or developing

00:34:10.929 --> 00:34:12.980
that creative idea
into something real

00:34:12.980 --> 00:34:15.550
that you and the rest of
the world can experience

00:34:15.550 --> 00:34:19.030
or divergent thinking
and convergent thinking.

00:34:19.030 --> 00:34:21.909
And divergent thinking
and convergent thinking

00:34:21.909 --> 00:34:24.610
are very straightforward
to understand.

00:34:24.610 --> 00:34:31.150
Divergent thinking is taking
some known object or event

00:34:31.150 --> 00:34:34.449
in the world or
sport or concept.

00:34:34.449 --> 00:34:35.409
It could be running.

00:34:35.409 --> 00:34:36.940
It could be a musical note.

00:34:36.940 --> 00:34:38.170
It could be jumping.

00:34:38.170 --> 00:34:42.460
It could be a particular
color on a piece of paper.

00:34:42.460 --> 00:34:47.320
And asking yourself how
many different things

00:34:47.320 --> 00:34:49.297
could that thing actually be.

00:34:49.297 --> 00:34:51.130
And you might say, well,
running is running.

00:34:51.130 --> 00:34:53.650
But let's use divergent
thinking as a way

00:34:53.650 --> 00:34:55.659
to illustrate what
divergent thinking is.

00:34:55.659 --> 00:34:57.508
If I show you a picture
of somebody running,

00:34:57.508 --> 00:34:58.300
I say, what do you.

00:34:58.300 --> 00:35:00.190
See and you say I
see somebody running.

00:35:00.190 --> 00:35:03.160
And then I might give you
a divergent thinking task

00:35:03.160 --> 00:35:04.840
and these tasks
are the same ones

00:35:04.840 --> 00:35:06.103
used in various experiments.

00:35:06.103 --> 00:35:08.020
And I'd say, how many
different things can you

00:35:08.020 --> 00:35:11.530
think about based on
this picture that you

00:35:11.530 --> 00:35:12.910
see of somebody running.

00:35:12.910 --> 00:35:15.860
Now, if you are able to
engage divergent thinking,

00:35:15.860 --> 00:35:18.730
you could say
running to the store.

00:35:18.730 --> 00:35:20.650
Running away from a lion.

00:35:20.650 --> 00:35:22.690
Running towards somebody I love.

00:35:22.690 --> 00:35:25.810
Or maybe you have a more
elaborate imagination

00:35:25.810 --> 00:35:29.410
and you could say,
running in front of a bus

00:35:29.410 --> 00:35:32.080
to grab a kid so the kid
doesn't get hit by the bus.

00:35:32.080 --> 00:35:34.180
Or running toward a
concert because I'm

00:35:34.180 --> 00:35:36.070
so excited about the
particular concert

00:35:36.070 --> 00:35:37.850
and then it starts to
spool into a story.

00:35:37.850 --> 00:35:39.880
In other words,
divergent thinking

00:35:39.880 --> 00:35:43.600
involves taking one simple what
we would call a neuroscience

00:35:43.600 --> 00:35:47.200
or psychology stimulus, one
image, or sound, et cetera

00:35:47.200 --> 00:35:49.240
and trying to
radiate out from that

00:35:49.240 --> 00:35:56.200
as many different divergent
situations, properties,

00:35:56.200 --> 00:36:01.090
characteristics, events, things
from that one specific element.

00:36:01.090 --> 00:36:03.820
So any divergent thinking task
would involve exactly that.

00:36:03.820 --> 00:36:08.020
I'd show you pictures or play
you sounds or words or notes

00:36:08.020 --> 00:36:11.260
or describe to you
events in history

00:36:11.260 --> 00:36:14.170
and try and see how many
things can radiate out

00:36:14.170 --> 00:36:18.670
from that in to diverse,
diverse, even distant types

00:36:18.670 --> 00:36:20.160
of concepts and pictures.

00:36:20.160 --> 00:36:20.660
OK.

00:36:20.660 --> 00:36:22.100
So that's divergent thinking.

00:36:22.100 --> 00:36:23.950
Divergent thinking
is really the process

00:36:23.950 --> 00:36:26.170
that underlies idea generation.

00:36:26.170 --> 00:36:29.380
And the basis of
divergent thinking

00:36:29.380 --> 00:36:32.170
is that more than
one idea is correct.

00:36:32.170 --> 00:36:35.560
In fact, the more ideas that
you have about one thing,

00:36:35.560 --> 00:36:37.570
the better your
divergent thinking.

00:36:37.570 --> 00:36:40.690
So if I were to give you
three minutes to list off

00:36:40.690 --> 00:36:43.787
all the things you can think
about related to this pen

00:36:43.787 --> 00:36:44.620
that I'm holding up.

00:36:44.620 --> 00:36:45.760
For those of you listening
I'm just holding up

00:36:45.760 --> 00:36:47.230
a pen in front of me.

00:36:47.230 --> 00:36:48.970
You just write them
out or say them out.

00:36:48.970 --> 00:36:51.623
Over the next 3 minutes
that would be an example

00:36:51.623 --> 00:36:52.540
of divergent thinking.

00:36:52.540 --> 00:36:55.595
However, if you just said
black pen, red pen, white pen,

00:36:55.595 --> 00:36:57.970
green pen, et cetera, that's
not very divergent thinking.

00:36:57.970 --> 00:37:01.010
It's only divergent in the
context of color space.

00:37:01.010 --> 00:37:03.130
And when I say space
that's just a nerd

00:37:03.130 --> 00:37:05.680
speak for one particular
domain of thinking.

00:37:05.680 --> 00:37:10.000
Whereas if you said
red pen, white pen,

00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:13.540
essay pen in a door
to hold the door

00:37:13.540 --> 00:37:15.940
open so that someone can
return to a building.

00:37:15.940 --> 00:37:18.250
And you started spooling
off a story related to that

00:37:18.250 --> 00:37:20.320
and why that was important,
well, there you go.

00:37:20.320 --> 00:37:23.170
Divergent thinking is
essentially taking one element

00:37:23.170 --> 00:37:24.942
and coming up with
many, many answers.

00:37:24.942 --> 00:37:26.650
And in the context of
divergent thinking,

00:37:26.650 --> 00:37:29.320
any answer goes, but
as we'll soon learn,

00:37:29.320 --> 00:37:32.140
not every answer is
interesting and relevant

00:37:32.140 --> 00:37:35.530
that is not every answer help
solve something or reveal

00:37:35.530 --> 00:37:37.030
something fundamental
and therefore,

00:37:37.030 --> 00:37:40.697
not every divergent
answer is truly creative.

00:37:40.697 --> 00:37:42.280
The other aspect of
divergent thinking

00:37:42.280 --> 00:37:43.960
that's really
important to understand

00:37:43.960 --> 00:37:49.120
is that the selection criteria
are extremely vague and vast.

00:37:49.120 --> 00:37:50.560
That is, there
are no constraints

00:37:50.560 --> 00:37:51.860
on what you come up with.

00:37:51.860 --> 00:37:53.770
So if I hold up this
pen and you say,

00:37:53.770 --> 00:37:58.630
orangutan, that's a perfectly
valid divergent idea

00:37:58.630 --> 00:38:00.580
from this pen because
you thought of it

00:38:00.580 --> 00:38:01.750
and it's distantly related.

00:38:01.750 --> 00:38:05.470
However, we have to
remember our earlier rule.

00:38:05.470 --> 00:38:11.230
If black pen and orangutan are
not linked up in our brain,

00:38:11.230 --> 00:38:13.660
in the observer's brain
in any meaningful way,

00:38:13.660 --> 00:38:16.185
it's only interesting
to you because you

00:38:16.185 --> 00:38:17.560
are the only one
that understands

00:38:17.560 --> 00:38:22.330
the rule that underlies the link
between this pen and orangutan.

00:38:22.330 --> 00:38:25.480
Whereas if you come up with
something different that

00:38:25.480 --> 00:38:27.760
somehow tells me and
everybody else something

00:38:27.760 --> 00:38:29.500
interesting about
pens or orangutans,

00:38:29.500 --> 00:38:31.630
now that's a truly
creative idea.

00:38:31.630 --> 00:38:33.418
I don't have such
an example in mind

00:38:33.418 --> 00:38:34.960
but later I'll give
you some examples

00:38:34.960 --> 00:38:36.752
of how you can actually
March down the path

00:38:36.752 --> 00:38:39.730
of divergent thinking and
use that executive network

00:38:39.730 --> 00:38:41.620
to suppress certain
options to cross off

00:38:41.620 --> 00:38:45.970
certain answers because, again,
an answer is valid but not all

00:38:45.970 --> 00:38:48.670
valid answers are
interesting or useful.

00:38:48.670 --> 00:38:50.530
And you can cross
those off and arrive

00:38:50.530 --> 00:38:54.160
at the most interesting
and truly creative answer.

00:38:54.160 --> 00:38:56.450
A couple of more things
about divergent thinking.

00:38:56.450 --> 00:38:58.900
Divergent thinking largely
taps into the networks

00:38:58.900 --> 00:39:02.510
of the brain that are involved
in mental flexibility.

00:39:02.510 --> 00:39:05.950
So this is a different aspect
of our prefrontal cortex, which

00:39:05.950 --> 00:39:08.830
is not based on executive
function and our ability

00:39:08.830 --> 00:39:14.330
to reduce options but rather
areas of the prefrontal cortex

00:39:14.330 --> 00:39:17.300
that are available to
generate multiple options

00:39:17.300 --> 00:39:20.973
and actually suppress context
to forget that pens are just

00:39:20.973 --> 00:39:22.640
for writing, for
instance, and that pens

00:39:22.640 --> 00:39:24.500
can do other things
like hold a door open.

00:39:24.500 --> 00:39:27.005
It's really an
unusual use of a pen.

00:39:27.005 --> 00:39:28.880
Again, none of these
examples that I'm giving

00:39:28.880 --> 00:39:30.118
are particularly interesting.

00:39:30.118 --> 00:39:32.660
They're just designed to get
you to understand the underlying

00:39:32.660 --> 00:39:34.550
concept of divergent thinking.

00:39:34.550 --> 00:39:36.050
And then the last
thing I'd like you

00:39:36.050 --> 00:39:39.350
to know about divergent thinking
is that divergent thinking

00:39:39.350 --> 00:39:41.660
involves a exploration.

00:39:41.660 --> 00:39:45.140
It's a wandering through
of ideas that you already

00:39:45.140 --> 00:39:49.580
had in your library, in
your memory banks about pens

00:39:49.580 --> 00:39:52.130
and what pens
could be related to

00:39:52.130 --> 00:39:54.950
and what pens ought
not to be related to.

00:39:54.950 --> 00:39:57.680
So, again, what's really
important about creativity

00:39:57.680 --> 00:40:01.130
is that there has to be the
basic building blocks already

00:40:01.130 --> 00:40:02.310
existing within us.

00:40:02.310 --> 00:40:04.550
This is why it's so
important to understand

00:40:04.550 --> 00:40:07.670
that if you are somebody who
really seeks to be creative,

00:40:07.670 --> 00:40:10.280
you really do need to
be somebody who forages

00:40:10.280 --> 00:40:14.090
for information and structured
information in particular

00:40:14.090 --> 00:40:15.740
if you are to be creative.

00:40:15.740 --> 00:40:17.690
The architect
simply can't come up

00:40:17.690 --> 00:40:21.260
with incredible drawings
or plans for buildings

00:40:21.260 --> 00:40:23.480
without understanding how
buildings are put together

00:40:23.480 --> 00:40:25.808
in the various rules
that govern buildings.

00:40:25.808 --> 00:40:27.350
In other words, you
can't break rules

00:40:27.350 --> 00:40:28.640
that you don't understand.

00:40:28.640 --> 00:40:31.820
I think in movies,
especially, we

00:40:31.820 --> 00:40:35.420
have this idea in mind
of this limitless concept

00:40:35.420 --> 00:40:39.320
or that we have these hidden
geniuses that somehow have

00:40:39.320 --> 00:40:42.380
access to all the math
knowledge without ever having

00:40:42.380 --> 00:40:43.280
done any formal math.

00:40:43.280 --> 00:40:45.792
Actually I was flying
back from Texas recently

00:40:45.792 --> 00:40:47.750
and Good Will Hunting
was on somebody's screen.

00:40:47.750 --> 00:40:49.458
I don't tend to watch
movies on the plane

00:40:49.458 --> 00:40:51.270
very often, sometimes
but not often.

00:40:51.270 --> 00:40:52.850
And I was remembering
in that movie,

00:40:52.850 --> 00:40:58.130
you've got this math genius who
is a janitor at MIT, et cetera

00:40:58.130 --> 00:41:00.860
and apparently just has
access to all this knowledge.

00:41:00.860 --> 00:41:02.930
It's a wonderful concept.

00:41:02.930 --> 00:41:06.830
A very, very I would say
even exceedingly rare thing

00:41:06.830 --> 00:41:07.797
to occur in the world.

00:41:07.797 --> 00:41:09.380
Sure there are people
who seem to have

00:41:09.380 --> 00:41:12.240
a natural talent for mathematics
or for something else.

00:41:12.240 --> 00:41:15.590
But this idea that
there are incredible

00:41:15.590 --> 00:41:18.200
geniuses among us that
just spontaneously

00:41:18.200 --> 00:41:22.400
have so much knowledge, that's
by far the exception rather

00:41:22.400 --> 00:41:24.902
than the rule, of course, and
may not even actually exist.

00:41:24.902 --> 00:41:27.110
I'm sure someone will put
it in the comments examples

00:41:27.110 --> 00:41:28.040
where this actually exists.

00:41:28.040 --> 00:41:29.480
More often than
not, what you find

00:41:29.480 --> 00:41:33.260
is that people who have extreme
virtuosity in a given area

00:41:33.260 --> 00:41:36.320
put many, many years
into developing

00:41:36.320 --> 00:41:38.930
the basic substrates,
the basic building blocks

00:41:38.930 --> 00:41:40.490
of whatever it is
their craft happens

00:41:40.490 --> 00:41:42.260
to be where they
demonstrate virtuosity.

00:41:42.260 --> 00:41:43.927
So this is very
important to understand.

00:41:43.927 --> 00:41:48.860
Nonetheless, divergent thinking
is the critical element

00:41:48.860 --> 00:41:51.500
for initiating the
creative process.

00:41:51.500 --> 00:41:53.540
Again, thinking about
creativity as a verb.

00:41:53.540 --> 00:41:57.860
And divergent thinking involves
taking some starting point,

00:41:57.860 --> 00:42:00.200
in this case a pen,
and then radiating out

00:42:00.200 --> 00:42:03.080
from that in a fairly
unconstrained what biologists

00:42:03.080 --> 00:42:06.440
call a random walk just
wandering through your thought

00:42:06.440 --> 00:42:08.120
space and memory
space about what

00:42:08.120 --> 00:42:09.440
could be related to this pen.

00:42:09.440 --> 00:42:11.000
Now, on the flip
side of creativity

00:42:11.000 --> 00:42:15.380
is the implementation of
specific combinations of things

00:42:15.380 --> 00:42:18.500
and testing those to see whether
or not they are interesting,

00:42:18.500 --> 00:42:21.380
relevant, or delight
to us or other people

00:42:21.380 --> 00:42:24.590
or scare us or other people
or thrill us or other people.

00:42:24.590 --> 00:42:27.770
In other words, a testing
of whether or not there's

00:42:27.770 --> 00:42:30.590
some fundamental rule to emerge.

00:42:30.590 --> 00:42:32.870
Again, I'm going to repeat
this many, many times

00:42:32.870 --> 00:42:34.010
throughout this
episode and I'm not

00:42:34.010 --> 00:42:35.540
going to apologize for
that because I think

00:42:35.540 --> 00:42:38.000
it's so important to understand
that creativity is not just

00:42:38.000 --> 00:42:38.930
novel combinations.

00:42:38.930 --> 00:42:41.030
They are novel
combinations of things that

00:42:41.030 --> 00:42:42.650
reveal something fundamental.

00:42:42.650 --> 00:42:46.430
And that often pop out
to us if not every time

00:42:46.430 --> 00:42:48.800
certainly most of the time
that we see that thing.

00:42:48.800 --> 00:42:50.870
It almost never
seems to be the case

00:42:50.870 --> 00:42:54.140
that something truly creative
dulls in its expression.

00:42:54.140 --> 00:42:56.450
And that's because what
it's repeating to us

00:42:56.450 --> 00:42:59.060
over and over again is this
fundamental rule that normally

00:42:59.060 --> 00:43:01.040
we can't see or
hear or experience

00:43:01.040 --> 00:43:03.680
in the absence of
this creative act.

00:43:03.680 --> 00:43:07.730
So the second part of creativity
where things are tested

00:43:07.730 --> 00:43:10.850
and where truly creative
elements are discovered

00:43:10.850 --> 00:43:12.530
is in convergent thinking.

00:43:12.530 --> 00:43:14.210
And convergent thinking
is, as the name

00:43:14.210 --> 00:43:16.370
suggests, just the opposite
of divergent thinking.

00:43:16.370 --> 00:43:19.323
Convergent thinking
would be, for example,

00:43:19.323 --> 00:43:21.740
if I give you an image or I
tell you the following things,

00:43:21.740 --> 00:43:27.690
I say wing, water, an engine.

00:43:27.690 --> 00:43:29.610
The concept that I
happen to have in mind

00:43:29.610 --> 00:43:33.660
is that of a plane
that can land on water.

00:43:33.660 --> 00:43:36.120
Most planes don't
land on water or not

00:43:36.120 --> 00:43:37.830
intended to land on water.

00:43:37.830 --> 00:43:39.480
One would hope that
their plane doesn't

00:43:39.480 --> 00:43:41.230
land on water unless
it's a plane designed

00:43:41.230 --> 00:43:42.180
to land on water.

00:43:42.180 --> 00:43:45.690
But in this case, a plane
that can land on water

00:43:45.690 --> 00:43:52.110
is one of the very few answers
that can combine wing, water,

00:43:52.110 --> 00:43:53.730
and engine.

00:43:53.730 --> 00:43:55.140
I'm sure there
are other answers,

00:43:55.140 --> 00:43:57.390
there are other
convergent thinking modes

00:43:57.390 --> 00:43:59.860
that can take you to an
answer that would be valid.

00:43:59.860 --> 00:44:01.080
But there are not many.

00:44:01.080 --> 00:44:02.670
And here what's
really most important

00:44:02.670 --> 00:44:04.800
is that I'm not asking
you to spool out

00:44:04.800 --> 00:44:07.680
or to radiate out from
these three things.

00:44:07.680 --> 00:44:10.140
Rather, I'm asking you to
combine them in some way that

00:44:10.140 --> 00:44:12.330
makes sense in the real world.

00:44:12.330 --> 00:44:15.000
And indeed there are planes
that can land on water.

00:44:15.000 --> 00:44:18.493
And wing water and
engine combined

00:44:18.493 --> 00:44:20.160
within those things
they are fundamental

00:44:20.160 --> 00:44:23.130
features, they are in
fact, necessary but not

00:44:23.130 --> 00:44:26.050
sufficient for having a
plane that can land on water.

00:44:26.050 --> 00:44:26.550
OK.

00:44:26.550 --> 00:44:28.633
So that's just one example
of convergent thinking.

00:44:28.633 --> 00:44:30.360
And a convergent
thinking task would

00:44:30.360 --> 00:44:33.190
involve you being given
a list of two or three

00:44:33.190 --> 00:44:34.690
or maybe even five
different things.

00:44:34.690 --> 00:44:36.090
And then for each of
those two or three or five

00:44:36.090 --> 00:44:37.620
different things,
as quickly as you

00:44:37.620 --> 00:44:39.510
can to come up with
a single answer

00:44:39.510 --> 00:44:42.360
that binds all of those
in a real world concept

00:44:42.360 --> 00:44:45.840
that obey the laws of nature
or physics in some way.

00:44:45.840 --> 00:44:50.280
For instance, you can just come
up with some answer that said,

00:44:50.280 --> 00:44:53.790
a bird that swallowed
an engine and that

00:44:53.790 --> 00:44:54.960
happens to be a sea bird.

00:44:54.960 --> 00:44:57.240
You could come up with that,
but that actually is not

00:44:57.240 --> 00:45:00.580
something that happens or
is that very typical at all.

00:45:00.580 --> 00:45:03.750
And so it seems like a mishmash
of things that are really

00:45:03.750 --> 00:45:05.610
just designed for you
to try and accomplish

00:45:05.610 --> 00:45:07.360
an answer rather
than something real,

00:45:07.360 --> 00:45:09.070
such as a plane
that lands on water.

00:45:09.070 --> 00:45:09.750
OK.

00:45:09.750 --> 00:45:12.690
The point here is that
divergent thinking

00:45:12.690 --> 00:45:16.140
is one aspect of our
cognition, of our thinking.

00:45:16.140 --> 00:45:19.680
And convergent thinking
is a very distinct aspect

00:45:19.680 --> 00:45:20.910
of our cognition.

00:45:20.910 --> 00:45:23.610
In fact, one of the
critical requirements

00:45:23.610 --> 00:45:26.805
for convergent thinking is
also to access our memory banks

00:45:26.805 --> 00:45:28.680
and our understanding
about the outside world

00:45:28.680 --> 00:45:30.990
just as it were with
divergent thinking,

00:45:30.990 --> 00:45:35.160
but it requires more focus
and more persistence.

00:45:35.160 --> 00:45:37.560
In fact, if we were to
come up with a key rule

00:45:37.560 --> 00:45:39.150
for divergent
thinking, it would be

00:45:39.150 --> 00:45:42.120
you almost want to have just
enough focus to remember what

00:45:42.120 --> 00:45:45.270
the initial object or
thing that was mentioned

00:45:45.270 --> 00:45:48.240
was to keep that in mind
so that your answers don't

00:45:48.240 --> 00:45:49.620
become completely random.

00:45:49.620 --> 00:45:53.310
But the more distant and
everywhere in between that

00:45:53.310 --> 00:45:55.350
you can generate
answers that is,

00:45:55.350 --> 00:45:57.690
the things that are
very close to pens,

00:45:57.690 --> 00:46:01.470
black pen, red pen
versus pen and doorstop,

00:46:01.470 --> 00:46:03.060
pen acting as a doorstop.

00:46:03.060 --> 00:46:06.810
Those are-- one is
very close, red pen is

00:46:06.810 --> 00:46:09.750
very close to black pen,
doorstop is pretty far

00:46:09.750 --> 00:46:11.190
from black pen.

00:46:11.190 --> 00:46:12.510
So that's the idea.

00:46:12.510 --> 00:46:15.773
Is that you want to explore and
undergo a range of exploration

00:46:15.773 --> 00:46:17.940
of different ideas whereas
with convergent thinking,

00:46:17.940 --> 00:46:20.260
you're really trying to
bind these things together.

00:46:20.260 --> 00:46:23.640
And so the key element
for convergent thinking

00:46:23.640 --> 00:46:27.060
is the aspect of
persistence and focus.

00:46:27.060 --> 00:46:30.270
And that's why convergent
thinking in many ways

00:46:30.270 --> 00:46:32.550
feels harder than
divergent thinking.

00:46:32.550 --> 00:46:33.990
It feels like there's an answer.

00:46:33.990 --> 00:46:36.323
And I want to get the answer
right and I can't solve it.

00:46:36.323 --> 00:46:37.890
It's a puzzle and
it's a puzzle that

00:46:37.890 --> 00:46:39.990
relies on very
distinct brain circuits

00:46:39.990 --> 00:46:41.160
from divergent thinking.

00:46:41.160 --> 00:46:42.390
Which brain circuits?

00:46:42.390 --> 00:46:44.430
Well, that's what we're
going to describe next.

00:46:44.430 --> 00:46:45.805
And again, this
is not just going

00:46:45.805 --> 00:46:48.382
to be a list of different brain
circuits with different names

00:46:48.382 --> 00:46:50.340
doing different things,
that wouldn't be useful

00:46:50.340 --> 00:46:51.570
to you or to me.

00:46:51.570 --> 00:46:55.920
Rather, what you're about to
learn is truly incredible.

00:46:55.920 --> 00:46:59.460
What it is we're going to talk
about one single molecule--

00:46:59.460 --> 00:47:02.430
dopamine, which is a
molecule most typically

00:47:02.430 --> 00:47:05.100
associated with motivation
and desire and drive

00:47:05.100 --> 00:47:06.960
and feelings of
pleasure in some cases.

00:47:06.960 --> 00:47:10.828
But that actually resides
within four different networks

00:47:10.828 --> 00:47:11.370
in the brain.

00:47:11.370 --> 00:47:13.920
Today we're going to talk
about two of those networks.

00:47:13.920 --> 00:47:17.800
And dopamine acting
in one network

00:47:17.800 --> 00:47:20.890
directly underlies
divergent thinking.

00:47:20.890 --> 00:47:23.380
Whereas dopamine in
another brain network

00:47:23.380 --> 00:47:25.420
underlies convergent thinking.

00:47:25.420 --> 00:47:27.225
And if at this point
in this episode

00:47:27.225 --> 00:47:28.600
you're saying OK,
when am I going

00:47:28.600 --> 00:47:30.400
to get the tools to
understand creativity

00:47:30.400 --> 00:47:32.260
and how to be creative,
what I can assure

00:47:32.260 --> 00:47:34.630
you is that if you understand
divergent thinking which

00:47:34.630 --> 00:47:37.630
hopefully now you do, and you
can understand what convergent

00:47:37.630 --> 00:47:40.390
thinking is, and
you can understand

00:47:40.390 --> 00:47:44.170
that dopamine is responsible
for both divergent thinking

00:47:44.170 --> 00:47:47.290
and convergent thinking but
through separate pathways.

00:47:47.290 --> 00:47:50.170
Well, then if you can understand
how those two separate pathways

00:47:50.170 --> 00:47:53.140
work and how to engage
them differentially,

00:47:53.140 --> 00:47:58.070
therein lie the tools that you
can use both to explore ideas.

00:47:58.070 --> 00:48:01.600
In other words, find what it
is that could be creative.

00:48:01.600 --> 00:48:04.810
And then systematically
test each of those ideas

00:48:04.810 --> 00:48:06.400
for what is truly creative.

00:48:06.400 --> 00:48:08.590
That is what meets the
criteria for something

00:48:08.590 --> 00:48:11.620
that is novel and truly
useful and informs us

00:48:11.620 --> 00:48:15.170
about something that we've never
seen, heard, or felt before.

00:48:15.170 --> 00:48:17.770
Let's just take a moment to talk
about the incredible molecule

00:48:17.770 --> 00:48:19.510
that is dopamine.

00:48:19.510 --> 00:48:22.000
Many people are familiar with
dopamine from the concept

00:48:22.000 --> 00:48:24.880
of quote unquote
"dopamine hits," which

00:48:24.880 --> 00:48:28.750
is popular language describing
the feeling of pleasure

00:48:28.750 --> 00:48:32.320
that we get from pretty
much anything that we like

00:48:32.320 --> 00:48:34.450
or that we continue to
engage in repeatedly.

00:48:34.450 --> 00:48:36.408
So some people will talk
about the dopamine hit

00:48:36.408 --> 00:48:38.500
that they get from
somebody attractive

00:48:38.500 --> 00:48:41.565
that they like texting them back
or the dopamine hit that they

00:48:41.565 --> 00:48:43.690
get from social media or
the dopamine hit that they

00:48:43.690 --> 00:48:46.000
get from sugar or the dopamine
that they get from this

00:48:46.000 --> 00:48:47.080
or from that.

00:48:47.080 --> 00:48:49.660
To be honest, the
concept of dopamine hits

00:48:49.660 --> 00:48:53.032
is not one that I favor because
in general, whenever people

00:48:53.032 --> 00:48:54.490
talk about dopamine
hits, typically

00:48:54.490 --> 00:48:55.865
they are talking
about activities

00:48:55.865 --> 00:48:58.750
such as social media
for which dopamine

00:48:58.750 --> 00:49:00.820
may be involved at some level.

00:49:00.820 --> 00:49:04.450
But often it's the case
that the behavior associated

00:49:04.450 --> 00:49:06.220
with that thing in
this case, social media

00:49:06.220 --> 00:49:09.040
is more of the compulsive
nature rather than

00:49:09.040 --> 00:49:12.490
an active seeking of something
with positive anticipation.

00:49:12.490 --> 00:49:14.830
And that's really what
dopamine is about at least

00:49:14.830 --> 00:49:17.380
in the context of one of its
major functions in the brain.

00:49:17.380 --> 00:49:20.530
Dopamine is really about
motivation and desire

00:49:20.530 --> 00:49:22.300
and movement.

00:49:22.300 --> 00:49:24.160
And it makes sense why
motivation, desire,

00:49:24.160 --> 00:49:27.190
and movement would be
linked up through a common,

00:49:27.190 --> 00:49:30.340
in this case neuromodulator
or chemical like dopamine.

00:49:30.340 --> 00:49:32.980
Because throughout
evolution if we

00:49:32.980 --> 00:49:36.820
were excited for or motivated
to pursue something,

00:49:36.820 --> 00:49:39.970
we had to move in order
to get it, to obtain it.

00:49:39.970 --> 00:49:41.770
And in general, we
can frame dopamine

00:49:41.770 --> 00:49:43.425
under the umbrella
of dopamine tends

00:49:43.425 --> 00:49:44.800
to be involved in
neural circuits

00:49:44.800 --> 00:49:49.000
in the brain that are involved
in processes that are taking us

00:49:49.000 --> 00:49:50.920
beyond the confines of our skin.

00:49:50.920 --> 00:49:53.620
That is, they motivate us
to go do something in terms

00:49:53.620 --> 00:49:55.030
of action in the world.

00:49:55.030 --> 00:49:58.570
Now, that statement might
seem distantly placed

00:49:58.570 --> 00:50:00.377
from a discussion
about creativity,

00:50:00.377 --> 00:50:01.960
but as we'll learn
a little bit later,

00:50:01.960 --> 00:50:06.070
one of the most useful tools
for engaging creativity

00:50:06.070 --> 00:50:10.390
and becoming more creative is
to think about action elements

00:50:10.390 --> 00:50:11.440
within a narrative.

00:50:11.440 --> 00:50:14.260
That is, things that we
and others can do in order

00:50:14.260 --> 00:50:17.740
to discover new rules
through actual movement.

00:50:17.740 --> 00:50:19.480
That's a little bit cryptic.

00:50:19.480 --> 00:50:20.110
Forgive me.

00:50:20.110 --> 00:50:21.652
But I promise I'll
return to it later

00:50:21.652 --> 00:50:24.460
and I will make
it crystal clear.

00:50:24.460 --> 00:50:27.880
There are four major circuits
in the brain that use dopamine.

00:50:27.880 --> 00:50:30.450
Although I should mention,
there are additional circuits

00:50:30.450 --> 00:50:30.950
as well.

00:50:30.950 --> 00:50:32.883
In fact, your eye
even contains neurons

00:50:32.883 --> 00:50:34.300
that release
dopamine that control

00:50:34.300 --> 00:50:36.730
the sensitivity of your eye
at different times of day

00:50:36.730 --> 00:50:38.230
to light, et cetera.

00:50:38.230 --> 00:50:39.730
The four major
circuits in the brain

00:50:39.730 --> 00:50:41.290
that utilize
dopamine however, are

00:50:41.290 --> 00:50:43.395
used for four major purposes.

00:50:43.395 --> 00:50:44.770
And I'll describe
what those are.

00:50:44.770 --> 00:50:47.170
First of all is a
neural circuit that

00:50:47.170 --> 00:50:50.140
uses dopamine among other
things but certainly relies

00:50:50.140 --> 00:50:54.190
on dopamine in a critical way
to engage movement, including

00:50:54.190 --> 00:50:54.903
eye movements.

00:50:54.903 --> 00:50:56.320
And we will return
to eye movement

00:50:56.320 --> 00:50:59.140
to why they're so important
for understanding creativity

00:50:59.140 --> 00:51:02.390
and maybe even for generating
creativity a little bit later.

00:51:02.390 --> 00:51:04.240
The name of the
circuit, again, is less

00:51:04.240 --> 00:51:05.810
important than what it does.

00:51:05.810 --> 00:51:08.560
But the name of this circuit
for those that want to know

00:51:08.560 --> 00:51:11.530
is the so-called
nigrostriatal pathway.

00:51:11.530 --> 00:51:13.600
The substantia nigra
is a brain area

00:51:13.600 --> 00:51:16.420
that is very dark that
projects to an area

00:51:16.420 --> 00:51:17.853
called the dorsal striatum.

00:51:17.853 --> 00:51:19.270
It contains a bunch
of subregions.

00:51:19.270 --> 00:51:21.853
So, again, for those of you that
really geek out on this stuff

00:51:21.853 --> 00:51:24.633
great, you can learn these names
and retain them in your memory.

00:51:24.633 --> 00:51:26.800
If you don't care about
names, don't worry about it,

00:51:26.800 --> 00:51:27.910
just discard the names.

00:51:27.910 --> 00:51:30.220
But areas of the brain like
the caudate and putamen

00:51:30.220 --> 00:51:31.990
and the dorsal
striatum receive input

00:51:31.990 --> 00:51:33.760
from the substantia nigra.

00:51:33.760 --> 00:51:36.520
In neuroanatomy, when
we name something,

00:51:36.520 --> 00:51:40.600
we say the origin of that thing
and where it connects through.

00:51:40.600 --> 00:51:43.147
So nigrostriatal
tells you that there

00:51:43.147 --> 00:51:44.980
is a connection between
the substantia nigra

00:51:44.980 --> 00:51:46.630
because it came
first, nigrostriatal,

00:51:46.630 --> 00:51:48.430
and then striatal
is where it ends up.

00:51:48.430 --> 00:51:51.400
So nigrostriatal pathway is
involved in generating bodily

00:51:51.400 --> 00:51:52.240
movements.

00:51:52.240 --> 00:51:54.580
It's involved in eye movements.

00:51:54.580 --> 00:51:56.950
And it is actually
a brain area that's

00:51:56.950 --> 00:51:59.943
engaged when you
think about movement.

00:51:59.943 --> 00:52:02.110
You can just have a story
in your mind about walking

00:52:02.110 --> 00:52:04.225
or a story in your mind
about running or story

00:52:04.225 --> 00:52:05.440
in your mind about driving.

00:52:05.440 --> 00:52:06.790
This area is engaged.

00:52:06.790 --> 00:52:08.890
Very interesting brain area.

00:52:08.890 --> 00:52:10.172
So that's the first circuit.

00:52:10.172 --> 00:52:11.380
Very important to understand.

00:52:11.380 --> 00:52:13.090
And I'll tell you
right now, that

00:52:13.090 --> 00:52:16.000
is the brain circuit
that is engaged when

00:52:16.000 --> 00:52:19.390
you undergo divergent thinking.

00:52:19.390 --> 00:52:21.370
Now, that itself
should be interesting.

00:52:21.370 --> 00:52:23.290
Even if you don't remember
any of the names of the things

00:52:23.290 --> 00:52:25.240
I just told you, that
you have a brain circuit

00:52:25.240 --> 00:52:28.000
that even if you just
think about walking it

00:52:28.000 --> 00:52:28.930
becomes more active.

00:52:28.930 --> 00:52:31.880
And the dopamine is involved
in that brain activity.

00:52:31.880 --> 00:52:33.820
And if you recall,
divergent thinking

00:52:33.820 --> 00:52:38.620
involves taking a concept
as boring as a pen

00:52:38.620 --> 00:52:41.710
and thinking about
other concepts that

00:52:41.710 --> 00:52:45.670
could link up with that pen in
some way, logical or illogical.

00:52:45.670 --> 00:52:49.990
The bridge could be completely
abstract and really fantastical

00:52:49.990 --> 00:52:52.090
with a bunch of different
ideas in between.

00:52:52.090 --> 00:52:54.498
A pen acting as a doorstop
because of some situation

00:52:54.498 --> 00:52:56.290
where you need to run
down stairs in a fire

00:52:56.290 --> 00:52:57.915
and get back upstairs
quickly to rescue

00:52:57.915 --> 00:52:59.350
somebody, very divergent.

00:52:59.350 --> 00:53:03.150
Or as divergent as
black pen to red pen.

00:53:03.150 --> 00:53:05.700
But what's amazing is
that that same circuit

00:53:05.700 --> 00:53:09.690
is the one that's involved
in generating and thinking

00:53:09.690 --> 00:53:10.800
about physical movement.

00:53:10.800 --> 00:53:13.830
That turns out to be vitally
important for tapping

00:53:13.830 --> 00:53:15.100
into the creativity process.

00:53:15.100 --> 00:53:17.740
So really frame that up in your
mind or commit it to memory.

00:53:17.740 --> 00:53:20.460
Now, the second dopamine circuit
associated with creativity

00:53:20.460 --> 00:53:23.190
is the one associated with
convergent thinking, which,

00:53:23.190 --> 00:53:24.690
again, is the
thinking where there's

00:53:24.690 --> 00:53:26.810
a specific correct answer.

00:53:26.810 --> 00:53:29.460
It requires focus and
it requires persistence.

00:53:29.460 --> 00:53:31.470
And the name of that
circuit, again, the name

00:53:31.470 --> 00:53:32.950
isn't as important
as what it does.

00:53:32.950 --> 00:53:37.590
But the name of that circuit
is the mesocortical pathway.

00:53:37.590 --> 00:53:41.070
The mesocortical pathway
is involved in motivation

00:53:41.070 --> 00:53:44.090
and it has an emotional
component too.

00:53:44.090 --> 00:53:45.840
Now, it will become
clear in a few minutes

00:53:45.840 --> 00:53:47.970
why that emotional
component is vital.

00:53:47.970 --> 00:53:49.530
But this is a circuit
that originates

00:53:49.530 --> 00:53:53.160
in a brain structure called the
lateral ventral tegmental area.

00:53:53.160 --> 00:53:55.530
Again, a bunch of words you
can remember it if you want,

00:53:55.530 --> 00:53:58.140
lateral ventral
tegmental area or you

00:53:58.140 --> 00:53:59.520
can not worry about the name.

00:53:59.520 --> 00:54:01.380
And it connects to
the prefrontal cortex,

00:54:01.380 --> 00:54:03.310
that area just
behind the forehead.

00:54:03.310 --> 00:54:05.310
And this mesocortical
area is involved

00:54:05.310 --> 00:54:08.190
in motivation and emotion
and is critical for focus

00:54:08.190 --> 00:54:09.390
and persistence.

00:54:09.390 --> 00:54:11.910
It is distinct from
a very nearby area,

00:54:11.910 --> 00:54:16.080
just sitting right next door
the so-called mesolimbic area,

00:54:16.080 --> 00:54:20.080
which is involved in desire
and feelings of reward.

00:54:20.080 --> 00:54:22.440
And this is the area that
is associated more typically

00:54:22.440 --> 00:54:26.305
with addictive behaviors
or compulsive behaviors.

00:54:26.305 --> 00:54:27.930
We're going to leave
out the discussion

00:54:27.930 --> 00:54:29.970
about the mesolimbic
pathway for now

00:54:29.970 --> 00:54:33.270
because it's not critical
to divergent or convergent

00:54:33.270 --> 00:54:37.020
thinking and it's not critical
to the process of creativity

00:54:37.020 --> 00:54:38.682
at least as far as we know.

00:54:38.682 --> 00:54:40.890
But I mention it because it
is the third and the four

00:54:40.890 --> 00:54:41.820
dopaminergic circuits.

00:54:41.820 --> 00:54:43.890
And then the fourth
circuit certainly

00:54:43.890 --> 00:54:47.310
one I've never talked about
before on this podcast, which

00:54:47.310 --> 00:54:48.810
doesn't mean anything
except that we

00:54:48.810 --> 00:54:52.770
haven't gotten to it yet,
is that tuberoinfundibular

00:54:52.770 --> 00:54:53.430
pathway.

00:54:53.430 --> 00:54:54.990
And that is the
pathway associated

00:54:54.990 --> 00:54:56.910
with dopamine and
your pituitary gland

00:54:56.910 --> 00:54:59.760
and the release of
hormones, in particular

00:54:59.760 --> 00:55:01.068
that travel to the ovary.

00:55:01.068 --> 00:55:02.610
If you have ovaries
or to your testes

00:55:02.610 --> 00:55:04.777
if you have testes and
trigger the release of things

00:55:04.777 --> 00:55:07.290
like estrogen and
testosterone, et cetera.

00:55:07.290 --> 00:55:11.040
Dopamine is intimately
involved in that circuitry.

00:55:11.040 --> 00:55:13.500
Again, not the topic
of today's discussion.

00:55:13.500 --> 00:55:15.420
For today's discussion,
we want to remember

00:55:15.420 --> 00:55:17.010
that there's a
dopamine circuit called

00:55:17.010 --> 00:55:19.740
the nigrostriatal circuit,
which is involved in movement

00:55:19.740 --> 00:55:22.380
and divergent thinking.

00:55:22.380 --> 00:55:25.680
And that alone should set
a flag up for you like wow,

00:55:25.680 --> 00:55:27.930
just thinking about
new ideas has something

00:55:27.930 --> 00:55:30.240
to do with physical movement.

00:55:30.240 --> 00:55:36.340
And the dopamine circuit that is
the mesocortical pathway, which

00:55:36.340 --> 00:55:39.490
is the one that's associated
with motivation and emotion,

00:55:39.490 --> 00:55:41.950
and that's the one required
for persistence and focus

00:55:41.950 --> 00:55:43.460
for convergent thinking.

00:55:43.460 --> 00:55:46.270
Why am I telling you all
of this about dopamine?

00:55:46.270 --> 00:55:50.890
Well, it turns out that dopamine
creates a certain number

00:55:50.890 --> 00:55:55.778
of responses in the brain and
body when it is active in one

00:55:55.778 --> 00:55:57.070
or the other of these circuits.

00:55:57.070 --> 00:55:58.930
And just for sake
of simplicity, so

00:55:58.930 --> 00:56:03.550
I don't have to keep saying
nigrostriatal and mesocortical.

00:56:03.550 --> 00:56:05.740
Here going forward,
I'm going to talk

00:56:05.740 --> 00:56:07.570
about the dopamine
circuit that's

00:56:07.570 --> 00:56:09.460
associated with
divergent thinking

00:56:09.460 --> 00:56:11.110
or the dopamine
circuit associated

00:56:11.110 --> 00:56:12.235
with convergent thinking.

00:56:12.235 --> 00:56:14.110
And, again, divergent
thinking and convergent

00:56:14.110 --> 00:56:17.560
think are the two processes
that have to occur.

00:56:17.560 --> 00:56:20.175
Usually first divergent then
convergent thinking then

00:56:20.175 --> 00:56:21.550
back and forth
and back and forth

00:56:21.550 --> 00:56:23.740
in order to arrive at
something creative.

00:56:23.740 --> 00:56:25.475
Divergent thinking
is about exploration.

00:56:25.475 --> 00:56:27.850
Convergent thinking is about
testing things and coming up

00:56:27.850 --> 00:56:30.580
with things that are the
right answer that feel right.

00:56:30.580 --> 00:56:33.550
And we will better define what
right means a little bit later.

00:56:33.550 --> 00:56:37.570
But you already know
right in this context

00:56:37.570 --> 00:56:40.960
is when you have some
combination of elements

00:56:40.960 --> 00:56:42.760
or some idea or
some written passage

00:56:42.760 --> 00:56:45.190
or some music or
some physical action

00:56:45.190 --> 00:56:50.710
that you just know this is
really novel and really cool.

00:56:50.710 --> 00:56:54.550
Or people see it or
hear it or taste it

00:56:54.550 --> 00:56:56.830
and say, this is really
novel and really cool

00:56:56.830 --> 00:56:58.660
and they don't
necessarily know why.

00:56:58.660 --> 00:57:01.690
It's just different in
a way that feels true.

00:57:01.690 --> 00:57:04.900
